**Encryption Flow (client-side, browser only):**
```
User selects file
    ↓
Generate random AES-256-GCM key (Web Crypto API)
    ↓
Encrypt file bytes → ArrayBuffer
    ↓
POST encrypted blob to Next.js API route → Pinata → returns CID
    ↓
keccak256(CID + ownerAddress + timestamp) → docHash
    ↓
Wrap AES key with recipient's public key (ECDSA via ethers.js)
    ↓
POST wrapped key → backend KeyProxy (stored encrypted in DB)
    ↓
Call contract.createDocument(docHash, CID, docType, expiry, ipTimestamp)
    ↓ (Polygon Amoy tx)
Emit DocumentCreated event → audit trail starts
```

