## Security Requirements (Non-Negotiable)

> [!CAUTION]
> These are hard acceptance criteria — no milestone ships without them passing.

- Raw file bytes **never** leave the browser unencrypted — verified by network inspector
- AES encryption keys **never** stored in plaintext in any DB, log, or env variable
- Slither static analysis → **zero HIGH-severity** findings on all contracts
- Revoking access makes document inaccessible within **one block** (~2s on Polygon Amoy)
- `verifyIntegrity()` returns `false` if IPFS file is tampered
- Gas limits: `createDocument < 200,000 gas`, `grantAccess < 50,000 gas`
- No blockchain jargon in any user-facing UI copy

